      "content": "I understand the caveats regarding environment and culture, but for the purpose of a rigorous literature review, I need to account for the genomic side of the debate. There's a body of older, more controversial work—and even some contemporary fringe studies—that suggests specific selective pressures in different geographic regions might have influenced neurobiological traits. \n\nCould you look specifically at the arguments made within those specialized fields? For instance, are there any documented hypotheses regarding how different ancestral groups might show different variations in dopamine receptor genes or other neurobiological markers that are linked to social behaviors or aggression? Even if the consensus is skeptical, I need to outline the specific mechanistic claims being made in those papers.",
